From 32c2a38e4b72905cab25d2ceee13e806a47f2fc8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GGEZUS <coelho.b.ricardo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 18:05:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] feat(input): touchscreen tap and bottom-edge swipe
 gestures

Extend the touchscreen swipe patchset:

- 3-finger tap: all fingers down and up within 250ms without crossing
  the swipe threshold runs a configurable action (default:
  maximize-column). `tap-4 { ... }` overrides the action for taps with
  four or more fingers.
- Bottom-edge swipe: single finger starting within 48px of the bottom
  edge moving up past 40px runs a configurable spawn command
  (`touchscreen-edge-swipe`, default off). A grab swallows the rest of
  the gesture so surfaces under the finger don't get a stray drag.
- Vertical swipe is now direct manipulation on touchscreens: content
  follows the finger, instead of the touchpad-natural direction.
- debug-level logging for gesture decisions (niri builds with
  max_level_debug, so trace! was compiled out).
